{
 "id": "comprehension_health",
 "version": "1.1.0",
 "depends_on": ["intent", "conversation_turn_ring"],
 "capability_keys": ["comprehension_health", "self_optimisation_sense"],
 "description": "SELF-OPTIMISATION, sense side (2026-07-10). The deep-reader/comprehension process runs SHADOW on every daemon chat turn and mechanically records its own health onto each Message (world_adapter._write_comprehension_to_graph / _record_shadow_health, per CLAUDE.md's adapter-may-maintain-a-rolling-datum exception): speech_act_divergence + comp_kind/shadow_speech_act, shadow_latency_ms + a monotonic shadow_seq, and the Agent-level rolling shadow_latency_recent_avg. This seed is the gap_awareness TWIN for that data: it DECIDES (as graph rules, never Python) when a recorded deficiency is a SelfConcern worth filing, so the agent notices its own comprehension process's problems as ITS OWN gaps, the same way it already notices unresolved topics/reported deficiencies/self-account gaps. Two rules:\n\n(1) note_recurring_speech_act_divergence -- a SINGLE disagreement between the front end's comp_kind and the deep reader's shadow_speech_act is not yet a pattern (comp_kind is deliberately pragmatic in places, per the Wave-3 cutover note in world_adapter.py); RECURRENCE (>=3 Messages sharing the SAME (comp_kind, shadow_speech_act) pair) is the graph's own signal that something is systematically off, not noise. The recurrence count is a held Count/Filter Term over NodesOfType('Message') -- a graph decision, never Python arithmetic. Fires from exactly ONE canonical binding per pair (the EARLIEST divergent Message in the group, selected via the shadow_seq ordering datum: 'no other same-pair divergent Message has a smaller shadow_seq') so a threshold-crossing round can never mint more than one SelfConcern for the same pair even before the content-dedup guard would catch a LATER round's attempt -- both guards compose, belt and braces.\n\n(2) note_comprehension_latency_gap -- a HealthNorm{metric, ceiling} node (seed data below) holds the latency BELIEF the rule compares the Agent's own shadow_latency_recent_avg against: the threshold is data the agent could later revise (teach() a new ceiling), never a Python literal. Fires once per crossing (content-deduped), from the single canonical 'latest shadow-read Message' binding (same shadow_seq trick, applied to ALL shadow-read messages rather than only divergent ones).\n\nBoth mint SelfConcern{status:'noted', source:'implicit', kind:'comprehension'|'performance', content:<data>} -- the SAME node shape gap_awareness.json mints, so the existing human-gated promote pipeline (scripts/jabberwock_daemon.py::promote_self_concern -> StandingConcern) and surfacing reader (reflective_faculty._run_self_gaps, 'what gaps do you have?') both find these gaps for free, no new plumbing. seeds/self_optimisation.json is the LAB twin: it gives the promoted 'performance'/'comprehension' concern's self-experiment an EFFICIENCY objective once it reaches the conversation experiment world. || v1.0.1 (2026-10-10, long-session cost): note_comprehension_latency_gap evaluates its cheap conditions (rolling average present and above the held ceiling, concern not yet filed) BEFORE the scan over all Messages for the latest shadow_seq. Measured: that scan ran for every received message on every re-match (0.9 ms/turn at turn 25, 190 ms/turn at turn 150). The where clause is a pure conjunction; the order does not change which bindings fire. || v1.1.0 (2026-10-10, conversation turn ring): the recurrence rule reads a TurnShape tally and its oldest member, and the latency rule compares with agent.latest_shadow_seq, instead of scanning every Message (scripts/gen_comprehension_health_shapes.py).",
 "nodes": [
  {
   "local_id": 1,
   "type": "HealthNorm",
   "attrs": {
    "metric": "shadow_latency_ms",
    "ceiling": 50.0,
    "description": "belief: the shadow-read comprehension pass should average under 50ms/turn on the held conversation corpus; a held, revisable threshold -- not a Python literal."
   }
  }
 ],
 "edges": [],
 "productions": [],
 "rules": [
  {
   "name": "tally_divergence_class",
   "comment": "Fold an attended shallow/deep reader disagreement into its class TurnShape (the conceptual tier the recurrence rule reads).",
   "match": [
    [
     "agent",
     "received",
     "m"
    ]
   ],
   "where": {
    "type": "And",
    "items": [
     {
      "type": "Eq",
      "a": {
       "type": "Attr",
       "node": {
        "type": "Var",
        "name": "m"
       },
       "key": "speech_act_divergence"
      },
      "b": {
       "type": "Lit",
       "value": 1.0
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "Not",
      "arg": {
       "type": "Eq",
       "a": {
        "type": "Attr",
        "node": {
         "type": "Var",
         "name": "m"
        },
        "key": "divergence_tallied"
       },
       "b": {
        "type": "Lit",
        "value": 1
       }
      }
     }
    ]
   },
   "effects": [
    [
     "add_node_if_absent",
     "sh",
     "TurnShape",
     {
      "shape_kind": "divergence",
      "sig_comp_kind": {
       "__term__": {
        "type": "IfThenElse",
        "cond": {
         "type": "Eq",
         "a": {
          "type": "Attr",
          "node": {
           "type": "Var",
           "name": "m"
          },
          "key": "comp_kind"
         },
         "b": {
          "type": "Lit",
          "value": null
         }
        },
        "then": {
         "type": "Lit",
         "value": ""
        },
        "other": {
         "type": "Attr",
         "node": {
          "type": "Var",
          "name": "m"
         },
         "key": "comp_kind"
        }
       }
      },
      "sig_shadow_speech_act": {
       "__term__": {
        "type": "IfThenElse",
        "cond": {
         "type": "Eq",
         "a": {
          "type": "Attr",
          "node": {
           "type": "Var",
           "name": "m"
          },
          "key": "shadow_speech_act"
         },
         "b": {
          "type": "Lit",
          "value": null
         }
        },
        "then": {
         "type": "Lit",
         "value": ""
        },
        "other": {
         "type": "Attr",
         "node": {
          "type": "Var",
          "name": "m"
         },
         "key": "shadow_speech_act"
        }
       }
      }
     }
    ],
    [
     "add_edge",
     "agent",
     "has_turn_shape",
     "sh"
    ],
    [
     "add_edge",
     "sh",
     "has_member",
     "m"
    ],
    [
     "add_edge",
     "m",
     "member_of",
     "sh"
    ],
    [
     "set_attr",
     "m",
     "divergence_tallied",
     1
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "mark_divergence_shape_first_member",
   "comment": "The oldest member of a divergence TurnShape is its first_member (the turn the concern names), marked while that turn is attended; loaded right after the tally so one pass folds, marks and files.",
   "match": [
    [
     "agent",
     "received",
     "m"
    ],
    [
     "m",
     "member_of",
     "sh"
    ]
   ],
   "where": {
    "type": "And",
    "items": [
     {
      "type": "Eq",
      "a": {
       "type": "Attr",
       "node": {
        "type": "Var",
        "name": "sh"
       },
       "key": "shape_kind"
      },
      "b": {
       "type": "Lit",
       "value": "divergence"
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "Not",
      "arg": {
       "type": "Exists",
       "source": {
        "type": "Neighbours",
        "node": {
         "type": "Var",
         "name": "sh"
        },
        "edge_type": "first_member"
       },
       "var_name": "_f",
       "predicate": {
        "type": "Lit",
        "value": true
       }
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "Eq",
      "a": {
       "type": "Var",
       "name": "m"
      },
      "b": {
       "type": "Argmin",
       "source": {
        "type": "Neighbours",
        "node": {
         "type": "Var",
         "name": "sh"
        },
        "edge_type": "has_member"
       },
       "var_name": "x",
       "value": {
        "type": "Var",
        "name": "x"
       },
       "default": null
      }
     }
    ]
   },
   "effects": [
    [
     "add_edge",
     "sh",
     "first_member",
     "m"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "note_recurring_speech_act_divergence",
   "match": [
    [
     "agent",
     "has_turn_shape",
     "sh"
    ],
    [
     "sh",
     "first_member",
     "m"
    ]
   ],
   "where": {
    "type": "And",
    "items": [
     {
      "type": "Eq",
      "a": {
       "type": "Attr",
       "node": {
        "type": "Var",
        "name": "sh"
       },
       "key": "shape_kind"
      },
      "b": {
       "type": "Lit",
       "value": "divergence"
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "Eq",
      "a": {
       "type": "Attr",
       "node": {
        "type": "Var",
        "name": "m"
       },
       "key": "speech_act_divergence"
      },
      "b": {
       "type": "Lit",
       "value": 1.0
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "Not",
      "arg": {
       "type": "Eq",
       "a": {
        "type": "Attr",
        "node": {
         "type": "Var",
         "name": "m"
        },
        "key": "divergence_health_noted"
       },
